Z||000000||Black88GT||11-20-2000||08:26 PM||||Seems I have a coolant leak on the drivers side coolant pipe, the ones the runs on the side around the doors.  Its right where they are welded.  Do you guys think a simple welding will help or should I replace it?  Anyone have them for sale? (mike v.?)<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-20-2000||09:26 PM||||Jeff,<P>You may be able to weld it up, but you will need to remove the coolant.  You won't be able to get a good weld with fluid inside the pipe....trust me, I've tried this!<P>I also, of course, have a few of these for sale if you find out yours isn't repairable. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||GT-maniac||04-29-2001||11:55 AM||||Did you ever get this fixed ? I have to replace my coolant pipe on the drivers side.<BR>I found a near mint one at a wreckers from a 4 banger which will have to be cut at the engine compartment end as it a little long. I had to cut the old pipe to get it out and it looks like I'm going to have to drop at least one side of the front supension to get the new pipe in. How did your fix go ?. I'd rather not have to do this again if I can avoid it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||04-29-2001||02:51 PM||||I got a friend to weld it for me, however I am getting replacement coolant tube brackets powder coated so I won't have to worry about them rusting away.  <P>I'm sure someone here can help you with the replacement, also as a side note Rodney Dickman sells stainless steel replacements, might want to check it out.<BR>||||reg||1
